                    <h3>General</h3>
                    <h4>Information</h4>
                    <p>This page serves as a brief example and testing ground for BAT tables. Feel free to play around with the table on the right, it will have no affect on the system.</p>

                    <p>Some tables will have more options and buttons, such as adding new entries, but these will be based on the rights you have for those pages.</p>

                    <h4>State</h4>
                    <p>Most BAT tables will save their state. This means that you can do a variety of customization, search, and more without losing your input when you leave the page. To reset the state of a table, click the 
                        <span><button class="btn btn-sm btn-bat-primary"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-rotate-ccw-icon lucide-rotate-ccw"><path d="M3 12a9 9 0 1 0 9-9 9.75 9.75 0 0 0-6.74 2.74L3 8" /><path d="M3 3v5h5" /></svg></button></span>
                        button
                    </p>

                    <h4>Column Reordering</h4>
                    <p>Column order can be personalized for your own workflow and experience. To move columns, click and drag the header and move it to wherever you want.</p>

